Phase 1: the DF-tree filesystem walker (#7)

SELECT the master file, probe every SIM-family identifier underneath,
descend into the dedicated files, and hand back a typed tree that
issue #9's scan serialises.

Absent and forbidden are separate variants of walk::NodeState with no
shared payload, and only a status word the caller has put in
walk::StatusMeaning is classified at all. 6A 82 is the one entry this
repository has verified; everything else reaches the caller as
NodeState::Refused carrying its status word verbatim, so a card that
answers a protected file differently from a missing one produces a
finding rather than a guess.

The traversal is an explicit stack, not recursion. Candidates are
de-duplicated per directory so a path can be reached at most once, and
a card describing an infinite tree is stopped by max_depth, max_nodes
and max_directories, each reported as a Note::Limit rather than applied
silently. A child whose identifier repeats one on its own path is NOT
treated as a cycle: a file identifier is unique inside a directory and
not across a card, so stopping there would hide legal files. It is
recorded as Note::RepeatedAncestor and descended.

Cards this project cannot control are the design premise, so nothing
reaches a panic and nothing reaches an unbounded allocation: every
response body goes through tlv::Stream and fcp::Template before it is
read, a malformed template is a Note and a node with empty
capabilities, and a response that is not a response stops the walk with
Error::Session.

Enumeration is by probing, because EF.DIR is not available on the
fixture: swSIM's GET RESPONSE rejects any P1 other than 00 [V], swicc
421c8cdd, and the 3GPP directory read is GET RESPONSE with P1 81.
Addressing is SELECT by path from the MF by default, because SELECT by
file identifier resolves globally on swSIM [V] and would produce a tree
that is not the card's directory structure.

tests/card_fixture.rs gains walks_the_file_system_of_a_real_card, which
runs the walker against swSIM and asserts it terminates, finds the MF,
reaches DF.GSM and the elementary files, reads EF.ICCID's real size
through the swICC tag table, and reports nothing forbidden - the last
because swICC evaluates no access condition on SELECT and therefore
cannot produce that status. The card-fixture workflow now runs both
card-backed tests and greps the walker's own log lines, so a green job
means the walk happened.

